# Neo Step parameters (docs/specs/neo-patch.md §3). The order is permanent: songs and presets store values by position.
# Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoStep
namespace NeoBuzz.Step
class NeoStepMachine
summary A step sequencer for values: 1 to 32 steps, each a level from 0 to 100 %, played at a synced rate with swing, a glide between steps and a random amount. It moves up to 8 parameters of other machines, each with its own depth, polarity, range and curve. Use it for stepped filter patterns, rhythmic gain and pan moves, and melodic control of any value, effects included.

group Pattern
Steps     "Steps"       1 32 8   int 0                          | How many steps the pattern has (1 … 32)
    id steps
    how Sets how many steps the pattern runs before it repeats, from 1 to 32.
    sound Different step counts against the song's bars make the pattern shift against the beat.
Rate      "Rate"        0 8 4    enum 1/2 1/4 1/8 1/16 1/32 1/2_dotted 1/4_dotted 1/8_dotted 1/16_dotted | How long each step lasts at the song's tempo
    id rate
    how Sets how long each step lasts, from 1/2 down to 1/32, straight or dotted.
    sound Faster rates make a busier pattern; dotted rates lilt against the beat.
Glide     "Glide"       0 1000 0 pct                           | How much of each step is spent gliding to its level
    id glide
    how Glides from one step's level to the next over up to a whole step.
    sound At 0 % the steps jump; higher values slide between them like a ramp.
Random    "Random"      0 1000 0 pct                           | Blends each step toward a random level
    id random
    how Mixes each step's level toward a fresh random level, by this amount.
    sound At 0 % the pattern repeats exactly; at 100 % every step is random.
Swing     "Swing"       0 750 0  pct                           | Delays every second step by up to 75 % of a step
    id swing
    how Delays every second step, up to three quarters of a step.
    sound The pattern gets a shuffled, off-beat feel.
WriteGlide "Write glide" 0 1000 408 time 0.001 1               | Time a target takes to cross its whole range: no write moves further than this allows
    id write_glide
    how Limits how fast a target may move: it takes at least this long to cross its whole range.
    sound A short glide keeps fast steps clean; a long one smooths them into slow sweeps.

group Levels
S1        "Step 1"  0 1000 1000 pct                          | Level of step 1, 0 … 100 %
    id step_1
    how Sets the level of step 1, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound The targets move to this level while step 1 plays.
S2        "Step 2"  0 1000 500 pct                          | Level of step 2, 0 … 100 %
    id step_2
    how Sets the level of step 2, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound The targets move to this level while step 2 plays.
